{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For it is double the hire of a hireling.</b> And according to this law, it would follow that if he [the slave] was ill for three years, he [the master] need not make up [the lost work], because there is in this a monetary payment that he has already given him. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Kiddushin 15a), and this is their language: From here they said — a hireling works by day, a slave by day and by night — end of quote. And this is a halakhah alluded to in Scripture."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:34.381945692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}